---
const points = [
  'AI should reduce friction, not remove accountability.',
  'Critical output needs review.',
  'The workflow should show what AI changed and why.',
  'The user should always know the next action.',
  'Automation is only useful when the process is understood.',
];
---

<section class="rounded-[1.55rem] border border-accent/24 bg-[linear-gradient(145deg,rgba(220,232,223,0.72),rgba(255,250,241,0.95))] p-6 md:p-8">
  <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] lg:items-start">
    <div>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-accent">Human approval</p>
      <h2 class="mt-5 font-display text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.02] text-brand md:text-6xl">
        AI drafts. People approve.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-base leading-relaxed text-brand/70 md:text-lg">
        Good AI workflows are often not fully automated. AI can collect, structure, classify and draft. People approve, correct and take responsibility where quality, risk, tone or decisions matter.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-3">
      {points.map((point, index) => (
        <div class="grid gap-4 rounded-xl border border-brand/10 bg-canvas/64 p-4 md:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
          <p class="font-mono text-[0.72rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-medium leading-relaxed text-brand/76">{point}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
